# Pin the public registry for this repo only.
#
# Machine-level registry configuration in ~/.npmrc is deliberately left alone -- other
# projects on a given machine may need a mirror. Without a pin here, `npm install` on a
# machine configured against a private mirror rewrites every `resolved` URL in
# package-lock.json to that mirror's hostname. Those URLs are meaningless to anyone else
# (and to CI), and they leak internal infrastructure names into a public repository's
# history, which no later commit can undo.
#
# Reads are unaffected either way -- npm substitutes the configured registry host when
# resolving `resolved` entries -- so this pin costs nothing and only constrains what gets
# written.
#
# GOTCHA: an NPM_CONFIG_REGISTRY environment variable outranks this file. npm's precedence
# is cli > env > project .npmrc > user .npmrc, so on a machine that exports that variable
# this pin is silently ignored -- `npm config list` will show it as "overridden by env".
# If you are on such a machine, either unset it for the command
# (`env -u NPM_CONFIG_REGISTRY npm install`) or pass `--registry=https://registry.npmjs.org`
# explicitly. The lockfile-hygiene CI check is the backstop for when someone forgets.
registry=https://registry.npmjs.org
